## Common Operations

### Video Upload Flow
1. User uploads via API → Multer receives file
2. Video model created → Job queued
3. Transcoding job processes → Multiple resolutions
4. HLS playlist generated → WebTorrent created
5. Files stored (local or S3) → Video published

### Live Streaming Flow
1. RTMP stream received → Node Media Server
2. FFmpeg transcodes → HLS segments created
3. Segments streamed to viewers → Video.js player
4. Optionally saved as replay

### Federation Flow
1. Local activity occurs → ActivityPub object created
2. Job queued for broadcast → HTTP signed requests
3. Sent to follower inboxes → Remote instances process
4. Remote objects cached → Federation synchronized

